Damn it!

262
00:18:08,780 --> 00:18:12,140
That's strange.
Back then she was trembling with fear.

263
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:14,380
You said a boiling kettle, right?

264
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:17,280
A boiling kettle

265
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:22,340
Could it be...

266
00:18:22,340 --> 00:18:23,680
Ryo-chan

267
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:27,000
Ryo-chan

268
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:31,880
Ryo-chan

269
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:41,200
Senpai

270
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:42,700
What are you planning to do, Ryo-chan?

271
00:18:42,700 --> 00:19:06,240
!

272
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:06,760
Dorā!

273
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,140
Ow

274
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:17,560
Terminachan's...!

275
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:19,460
W-what happened?

276
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:20,480
Chief!

277
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:22,440
Just as I thought!

278
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:26,000
It wasn't the sound it's weak to,
it was fire!

279
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:27,060
I see!

280
00:19:27,180 --> 00:19:31,940
Nakagawa! Get every drop of gasoline in Kyoto with tanker trucks!
We're taking him down!

281
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:36,440
Idiot! What happens if you do that
and all of Kyoto goes up in a huge fire?

282
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:40,260
But this is an emergency,
so it can't be helped!

283
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:44,740
To the fuel depot!

284
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:47,340
I'll kill him!

285
00:20:01,940 --> 00:20:03,960
Yaa! Wait!

286
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:09,880
Hold on, I'm going in!

287
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:11,240
Yaa! Chaa!

288
00:20:17,140 --> 00:20:19,480
Right! Tank lorries from all over Kyoto!

289
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:23,260
Where to? Even if you ask where...

290
00:20:24,060 --> 00:20:25,360
Yes! Maria-chan!

291
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:26,700
Maria-chan, are you alright?

292
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:30,320
Yes, I was thrown and
crashed into a mountain, but...

293
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,460
It's Mount Daimonji.

294
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:36,640
Mount Daimonji?

295
00:20:37,120 --> 00:20:39,080
The Mount Daimonji from
the Daimonji bonfire?

296
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:40,040
That's it.

297
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:44,400
It's the only place in Kyoto
where you can light a big fire.

298
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:48,140
Tank lorries, second only to tanks.

299
00:20:48,140 --> 00:20:50,040
Our destination is Mount Daimonji!

300
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,680
Assemble at Mount Daimonji!

301
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:52,520
Repeat.

302
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:54,560
Our destination is Mount Daimonji!

303
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:01,260
Enough already, Reiko.

304
00:21:33,300 --> 00:21:35,800
Tank lorries are
gathering at Mount Daimonji.

305
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:39,920
Senpai, please lure the
Terminator to Mount Daimonji.

306
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:41,220
Then we're counting on you.

307
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:42,780
Hey, you!

308
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:44,940
Take Pen with you!

309
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:57,800
Alright!

310
00:21:58,480 --> 00:21:59,520
We're ready to go.

311
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:01,220
Senpai, we're counting on you.

312
00:22:06,020 --> 00:22:07,920
Where's that Ryotsu guy?

313
00:22:09,100 --> 00:22:09,860
Here he comes.

314
00:22:11,420 --> 00:22:12,740
Just a little more.

315
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:21,080
Ryotsu!

316
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:21,980
Ryotsu!

317
00:22:21,980 --> 00:22:24,060
The tank lorries are just ahead.

318
00:22:24,060 --> 00:22:25,380
Okay, Ryotsu!

319
00:22:29,740 --> 00:22:31,700
Wait, Ryotsu!

320
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:35,960
The mountain road really
takes it out of you.

321
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:45,380
You can't escape now!

322
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:47,140
Crush them!

323
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:53,960
No way!

324
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:55,980
Wooo!

325
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:57,820
Yeah!

326
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:00,640
Uh, ugh!

327
00:23:00,860 --> 00:23:01,940
Alright!

328
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:04,880
Wh-what is this?

329
00:23:05,340 --> 00:23:06,620
Hahahaha!

330
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:09,140
Beep!

331
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:13,280
Yeah! Terminachan!
Your mom's got an outie belly button!

332
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:15,900
Free, free, free-free-free!

333
00:23:16,280 --> 00:23:18,560
Bakabon!

334
00:23:18,800 --> 00:23:20,900
Let's go home!

335
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:22,480
Wait up!

336
00:23:26,720 --> 00:23:29,460
Gotcha, Terminator!

337
00:23:29,460 --> 00:23:31,900
What? What's going on?

338
00:23:31,900 --> 00:23:33,340
It's like this.

339
00:23:33,340 --> 00:23:34,100
What?

340
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:58,520
Aaaaaaah!

341
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:06,340
Yes! We did it!

342
00:24:06,340 --> 00:24:06,480
Yeah.

343
00:24:09,140 --> 00:24:10,760
Lord Ryo!

344
00:24:10,760 --> 00:24:13,740
We called Maria! Yay!

345
00:24:13,740 --> 00:24:18,920
For Lord Ryo,
I'd walk through fire and water!

346
00:24:22,660 --> 00:24:25,340
Looks like this is all resolved.

347
00:24:26,860 --> 00:24:31,640
But I never expected to see the
Daimonji bonfire out of season.

348
00:24:36,540 --> 00:24:37,800
And that's a wrap.

349
00:24:37,800 --> 00:24:40,560
This will surely save
the future of the Earth.

350
00:24:40,560 --> 00:24:42,100
That was pretty easy.

351
00:24:42,620 --> 00:24:45,080
Well, thank you all for your cooperation.

352
00:24:46,280 --> 00:24:47,500
That's great.

353
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:50,640
Hey, my money really is
going to arrive, right?

354
00:24:50,640 --> 00:24:53,660
Yes, I think it'll arrive any moment now.

355
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:58,080
It looks like it's arrived.

356
00:25:03,380 --> 00:25:06,240
Well then, I'll be taking my leave.

357
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:07,900
Do take care.

358
00:25:07,900 --> 00:25:08,880
Take care of yourself.

359
00:25:09,600 --> 00:25:10,120
Thank you very much.

360
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:12,680
It's the money from the gold scrubber.

361
00:25:13,580 --> 00:25:15,620
With this, I'll be a big shot rich man.

362
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:18,100
That's not allowed.

363
00:25:18,100 --> 00:25:20,380
All of that money is confiscated.

364
00:25:20,380 --> 00:25:22,080
Why?

365
00:25:23,660 --> 00:25:26,460
Do you have any idea how much
damage you caused in Kyoto?

366
00:25:26,460 --> 00:25:29,080
That was all Terminachan's doing, though.

367
00:25:29,080 --> 00:25:30,600
This is my money.

368
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:31,200
No.

369
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:33,720
All of it will be used
for restoration costs.

370
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:34,220
That's right.

371
00:25:34,220 --> 00:25:35,200
Hey, keep it small.

372
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:36,840
Get another trillion yen ready.

373
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:37,880
Hey.

374
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:41,260
Wait, hold on!

375
00:25:41,260 --> 00:25:42,280
I said wait!

376
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:45,500
What's going on?

377
00:25:45,500 --> 00:25:48,020
Looks like the time warp entrance

378
00:25:48,020 --> 00:25:49,620
has been sealed off.

379
00:25:50,140 --> 00:25:50,540
N-no...

380
00:25:51,940 --> 00:25:52,340
That can't be...

381
00:25:53,980 --> 00:25:56,720
Meanwhile, in the year 2301 AD,

382
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:59,400
brought back from the 21st century

383
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:01,580
thanks to the Ryotsu GPX,

384
00:26:01,580 --> 00:26:04,960
the Earth regained its peace.

385
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:06,960
And they all lived happily ever after.

386
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:08,460
Like hell it's happily ever after!

387
00:26:08,460 --> 00:26:10,280
We went through all that effort for nothing!

388
00:26:10,280 --> 00:26:11,420
Pure profit for me!

389
00:26:24,960 --> 00:26:30,160
The afternoon sky, as if someone is watching

390
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:37,040
looking up as I turned back,
led by Daddy's hand

391
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:44,220
that strange feeling I had back then

392
00:26:44,220 --> 00:26:49,220
So the pebble I found
while crossing the road

393
00:26:49,220 --> 00:26:55,280
I kept kicking it all the way home

394
00:26:57,760 --> 00:27:03,520
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

395
00:27:04,420 --> 00:27:10,920
There are scary-faced priests
and kids with loose hearts too

396
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:16,400
Why don't you turn that corner over there

397
00:27:17,620 --> 00:27:21,600
You can meet everyone, everyone

398
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:26,420
Over there is Kameari

399
00:27:26,420 --> 00:27:30,460
It's surely Kameari

400
00:27:31,060 --> 00:27:34,780
Everyone, come on, to our town

